from pathlib import Path
p = Path('docs/parity/niri-gaps-layout-behaviour.md')
data = p.read_bytes()
nl = b'\r\n' if b'\r\n' in data else b'\n'
text = data.decode('utf-8').replace('\r\n','\n')
updates = {
'Column width = proportion of view or fixed logical px, kept when windows open/close': ('done (Lane G)', '`Column::width_proportion` / `width_fixed_logical` retain requested intent; `refresh_strip_widths` resolves it against the output view and DPI, without dividing established columns on admission/removal. `WindowSlot` and expel/new-column paths preserve it. Legacy explicitly configured equal-share mode remains an extension. Pure regressions in `engine/strip_model.rs`; live `h41_widths_survive_open_close`. See [Lane G report](lane-g-report.md).'),
'`gaps`': ('partial (Lane G)', 'niri `layout { gaps N; }` sets inner and outer gaps (`Decoder::decode_layout_into`); composed with signed struts by `tiling_work_rect`. Live `h40_gaps_and_signed_struts_compose` verifies actual visible-frame spacing. Existing border allocation adds the reserved border on both sides. Fractional/logical gaps at non-100% DPI still round to integer pixels; not claimed complete.'),
'`struts` (left/right/top/bottom, negative allowed)': ('partial (Lane G)', '`decode_layout_into` accepts signed sides; `LayoutConfig` stores i32, and `tiling_work_rect` uses bounded i64 arithmetic before converting extents, so negative struts expand instead of wrapping to an empty view. Pure contraction/expansion/oversized-strut regression; live `h40_gaps_and_signed_struts_compose` uses negative left and positive other sides. Fractional logical struts/per-DPI scaling remain open.'),
'`center-focused-column` never / always / on-overflow': ('done (Lane G)', '`Workspace::reveal_with_policy` / `reveal_focused_column` implement all three policies with negative leading space: minimal reveal for never, centering for always, centering only when a column overflows for on-overflow. Uses effective output config. Four pure strip-policy regressions; live `h40_never_keeps_visible_columns_still`, `h40_always_centres_first_middle_last`, `h40_on_overflow_only_centres_when_needed`.'),
'`always-center-single-column`': ('done (Lane G)', 'Bare flag or bool decoded and applied by `Workspace::reveal_with_policy`, independently of never/always/on-overflow. Empty strip is safe. Pure `single_column_can_center_in_never_mode`; live `h40_always_center_single_column`.'),
'`preset-column-widths` (proportion/fixed list)': ('done (Lane G)', 'niri mixed `{ proportion 0.5; fixed 800; }` list decoded into `SizeSpec`; tiled and floating cycles resolve effective output presets. Fixed sizes are logical window pixels (border added for tiles), proportions use the gap-aware view. Empty/unset list uses thirds/half/two-thirds. Pure mixed/wrap/nonpreset regression; live `h42_*`.'),
'`default-column-width` proportion / fixed / empty (window decides)': ('done (Phase 2A; Lane G)', 'Both `layout { default-column-width { ... } }` and the existing per-window rule act. `remember_column_width_spec` stores proportional/fixed-logical intent; `{}` retains admission geometry; a rule overrides the layout default. Decoder regressions cover all three forms. Earlier `h13_*` plus Lane G `h41_widths_survive_open_close` verify actual fixed/proportional widths.'),
'New window opens as a column right of the active one, becomes active, view animates to it': ('partial (Lane G)', '`Workspace::insert_window_after_active` replaces append-at-end for ordinary admission, inactive workspace rules and unfloat. It remembers/focuses the new tile; reveal uses the configured centering policy. Pure middle/end/empty insertion regression; live `h41_inserts_right_of_active_middle_end_empty`. Animation timing remains owned by the separate animation lane; H40-H44 deliberately disable animations.'),
'Active tile remembered per column; active column remembered per workspace': ('done (Lane G)', 'Each Column and Workspace stores an active window id, independent of the bounded MRU ring and stable across index changes. `Monitor::set_focus`, directional/first/last column focus and workspace restore consult/update that memory, falling back safely after removal. Pure regression exceeds the 32-entry MRU capacity; live `h41_column_remembers_active_stacked_tile` and `h41_workspace_remembers_active_column_and_tile`.'),
'`switch-preset-column-width`': ('done (Phase 1; Lane G)', 'The existing remembered-preset cycle now reads mixed configured `SizeSpec` presets, resolving fixed logical widths and proportions against the effective output view. A nonpreset takes the first configured wider size; the end wraps. Pure `mixed_presets_step_from_nonpreset_and_wrap_both_ways`; live `h42_mixed_presets_forward_and_wrap`, `h42_nonpreset_steps_to_next_wider`.'),
'`switch-preset-column-width-back`': ('done (Phase 1; Lane G)', 'The same configured mixed list in reverse, wrapping to the last preset; nonpreset widths take the last narrower preset. Live `h42_mixed_presets_backward_and_wrap` and the pure mixed-preset regression.'),
'Floating layer: per workspace, always above tiles, does not scroll, has its own focus': ('partial (Phase 1; Lane G verified)', 'Existing `float_homes`, `reconcile_floats` and `raise_floats` keep per-workspace geometry and re-raise floats above activated tiles without scrolling them. Existing H5 gates cover z-order, hide/show and workspace moves; Lane G `h43_float_does_not_scroll_with_tiles` / `h43_float_rectangle_survives_workspace_and_retile` exercise actual scrolling, workspace roundtrip and retiling. Dedicated focus-floating/focus-tiling layer actions remain open (separate lane).'),
'`open-floating` (true/false)': ('done (Phase 2A; Lane G)', 'Explicit true/false still controls rule placement; false also suppresses Lane G dialog auto-floating (`add_window_with_target`). Floats open at the requested rule size, centered, or retain startup geometry. Existing rule-resolution pure tests and H13 gates remain; `h43_owned_dialog_auto_floats_over_owner` verifies the new automatic default. Tool/child/system helper exclusions are unchanged.'),
'Auto-float for dialogs (parent), fixed-size windows': ('partial (Lane G)', '`should_auto_float` admits owned top-level popups and native #32770 dialogs, excluding child/tool/no-activate/system helpers. Normal top-level apps are not floated merely for lacking a thick frame. Unless placement rules override, a dialog follows its owner workspace/output and is centered on the owner; explicit `open-floating false` wins. Pure classification regression and live `h43_normal_toplevels_stay_tiled`, `h43_owned_dialog_auto_floats_over_owner`. Fixed-size non-dialog heuristics remain open; Windows rejection fallback remains.'),
'Native title-bar drag / resize of a tiled window is reconciled by the layout': ('done (Lane G; documented Windows approximation)', '`native_move_resize_start` cancels the HWND animation and gives the native modal loop exclusive geometry ownership; tile/float placement skips it until end. End reads the unthrottled live visible frame, invalidates applied state, adopts fixed-logical column width and the resized stacked tile height (siblings get remaining allocation), or remembers float geometry. Caption-only moves snap back to the same slot; no compositor-style reorder is claimed. Four pure regressions plus real caption/border drags `h44_*`, including refresh during the held loop and after drop; see [Lane G report](lane-g-report.md).'),
}
for key,(status,evidence) in updates.items():
    prefix = '| '+key+' |'
    matches = [line for line in text.splitlines() if line.startswith(prefix)]
    if len(matches)!=1: raise RuntimeError((key,len(matches)))
    old = matches[0]
    cells = old.split(' | ')
    cells[3] = status
    cells[4] = evidence
    text = text.replace(old,' | '.join(cells),1)
p.write_bytes(text.replace('\n',nl.decode()).encode('utf-8'))
